#. Tag: title
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working With the Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The state of a given breakpoint is indicated via the relevant text with a "
"different background color. You can choose the color desired: see the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Editor</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> dialog, on the <guilabel>Colors</guilabel> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set, disable or delete a breakpoint using keys, the <guimenu>Debug</"
"guimenu> menu or the buttons on the tool bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can move the cursor around the text using the following keys:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Arrow keys: <keysym>Left Arrow</keysym>, <keysym>Right Arrow</keysym>, "
"<keysym>Up Arrow</keysym> or <keysym>Down Arrow</keysym>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Page keys: <keycap>Page Up</keycap> or <keycap>Page Down</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working With &kxsldbg; Output"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most of the output from &kxsldbg; is captured and presented either in the "
"inspectors dialog or the &kxsldbg; output window. The exceptions to this "
"rule are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An error message that comes from &kxsldbg; is displayed inside a message "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The result of evaluating an expression is displayed in a message dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kxsldbg_mainwindow.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The output of search is sent to the file indicated in the &kxsldbg; output "
"window."
msgstr ""
